From f8835e6fa8edf8083dbeeba66e41e9aa30267541 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vuln Patch Pipeline <vuln-patch@chainguard.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:12:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bound isAlphaNumber and its regex helpers to 250 characters

PhoneNumberUtil.isAlphaNumber(CharSequence) passed caller text of any
length to isViablePhoneNumber and maybeStripExtension. These helpers
run VALID_PHONE_NUMBER_PATTERN and EXTN_PATTERN, which backtrack
polynomially on long non-matching input and recurse once per digit on
long digit runs (CWE-1333). A long string could hold a thread for
seconds or throw StackOverflowError. parse() already refuses input
longer than MAX_INPUT_STRING_LENGTH (250), but isAlphaNumber did not.

isViablePhoneNumber now returns false for text longer than 250
characters. maybeStripExtension returns "" and leaves the buffer
unchanged for text longer than 250 characters. Neither runs its
pattern on such text. isAlphaNumber also returns false above 250
before it copies the input or calls either helper. Input of 250
characters or fewer behaves as before. parse() is unchanged.

Adds AlphaNumberRedosTest.

Cgp-Finding: CGP-gcrw-87qp-x4c3
